⚠️ PROJECT LIMITATIONS

The following limitations should be considered when interpreting the results.

1. Missing Customer Identifier

The documented dataset does not include a dedicated customer ID or customer name.

Consequently, the project cannot reliably identify unique customers or track individual customer histories using the listed fields alone.

2. Discount Definition

The meaning of "Discount_Applied" must be confirmed. A currency amount and a percentage require different calculation logic.

3. Profit Formula

The current SQL script's profit calculation must be validated against the meaning and unit of "Cost Price" and "Quantity Purchased".

4. Transaction Identifier Quality

A repeated "Transaction_ID" should be investigated before deciding whether it is a duplicate that needs correction.

5. Data Accuracy

The quality of the analysis depends on the accuracy, completeness, and consistency of the source records.

6. Date-Based Analysis

Monthly and weekly comparisons require valid dates and suitable sorting logic.

7. Final KPI Values

Actual sales totals, profit totals, transaction counts, and other results must be taken from the validated data and final Power BI report. They should not be inferred from sample SQL queries.

